                                    {
                                        "__typename": "ParagraphText",
                                        "id": "273",
                                        "verticalAlign": false,
                                        "body": {
                                            "processed": "\u003Cp class=\u0022text-align-center\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022subhead color-accent\u0022\u003ESUCCESS\u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022text-align-center\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022h3\u0022\u003EImpact\u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022text-align-center\u0022\u003EThe portfolio became a working demonstration of the development practices it represents. The combination of Drupal 11, Next.js, TypeScript, REST API, GraphQL, GitHub, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, CI\/CD, and headless architecture created a scalable platform that separates content management from the front-end experience.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022text-align-center\u0022\u003EThe automated deployment infrastructure also transformed the site from a manually maintained project into a repeatable software delivery process. Code changes can move from GitHub through automated builds and testing into versioned development or production releases, with Drupal updates and deployment tasks handled through Jenkins.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022text-align-center\u0022\u003EThe result is both a portfolio website and a real-world example of modern web architecture, API integration, DevOps, automation, version control, and full-stack development.\u003C\/p\u003E\n"
